WEBVTT

00:00:09.418 --> 00:00:10.668
(GASPING IN RELIEF)

00:00:17.926 --> 00:00:19.176
(COUGHING)

00:00:20.095 --> 00:00:21.929
(THUNDER RUMBLING)

00:01:18.487 --> 00:01:19.528
(PICKETT STRUGGLING)

00:01:51.937 --> 00:01:53.771
They're ready for you, Newt.

00:01:56.024 --> 00:01:57.191
Leta.

00:01:59.486 --> 00:02:00.945
What are you doing here?

00:02:01.154 --> 00:02:04.156
Theseus thought it would be good
if I became part of the Ministry family.

00:02:05.367 --> 00:02:07.660
Did he actually say the words
"Ministry family"?

00:02:07.744 --> 00:02:10.121
- (LAUGHS)
- That sounds like my brother.

00:02:10.622 --> 00:02:11.956
(CLEANER APPROACHING)

00:02:27.848 --> 00:02:30.224
Theseus was disappointed
you couldn't come to dinner.

00:02:31.393 --> 00:02:33.144
Any of the nights we've asked you.

00:02:33.937 --> 00:02:35.229
NEWT: Well, I've been busy.

00:02:35.397 --> 00:02:38.691
LETA: He's your brother, Newt.
He likes spending time with you.

00:02:39.568 --> 00:02:41.110
And so do I.

00:02:45.157 --> 00:02:46.240
(PICKETT CHITTERS)

00:02:46.324 --> 00:02:48.659
Oi, you! Hop in, Pick.

00:02:50.370 --> 00:02:52.455
Why do strange creatures
love you so much?

00:02:52.706 --> 00:02:54.373
Well, there are no strange creatures.
Only blinkered people.

00:02:54.624 --> 00:02:56.125
Only blinkered people.

00:02:59.880 --> 00:03:03.048
How long did you get in detention
for saying that to Prendergast?

00:03:03.675 --> 00:03:05.634
I think it was a month that time.

00:03:05.802 --> 00:03:09.013
And I set off a Dungbomb under his desk
so I could join you. Do you remember?

00:03:14.644 --> 00:03:15.728
NEWT: Um...

00:03:15.812 --> 00:03:17.646
No, I actually don't remember that.

00:03:18.815 --> 00:03:20.107
THESEUS: Hello.

00:03:20.233 --> 00:03:23.444
Theseus. We were just talking
about Newt coming for dinner.

00:03:23.612 --> 00:03:25.029
Really? Well...

00:03:26.490 --> 00:03:27.865
Look, before we go in there, I...

00:03:28.116 --> 00:03:29.825
It's my fifth attempt, Theseus.
I know the form.

00:03:30.035 --> 00:03:32.661
This isn't gonna
be like the other times. This is...

00:03:32.829 --> 00:03:35.748
Just try and keep an open mind.
Will you?

00:03:36.666 --> 00:03:37.792
And maybe a little less...

00:03:38.043 --> 00:03:39.168
Like me.

00:03:40.670 --> 00:03:41.796
Well, it can't hurt.

00:03:42.714 --> 00:03:44.256
Come on, let's go.

00:03:51.014 --> 00:03:52.181
<i>TRAVERS: Hearing commences.</i>

00:03:53.475 --> 00:03:57.186
You want an end to the ban
on you traveling internationally.

00:03:57.979 --> 00:03:59.104
Why?

00:03:59.189 --> 00:04:00.898
Because I'd like
to travel internationally.

00:04:01.066 --> 00:04:06.403
Subject uncooperative and evasive
on reasons for last international trip.

00:04:06.571 --> 00:04:08.447
It was a field trip, sir.

00:04:08.615 --> 00:04:11.575
I was just collecting material
for my book on magical beasts.

00:04:11.910 --> 00:04:13.077
You destroyed half of New York.

00:04:13.328 --> 00:04:15.079
No, that's actually factually incorrect
on two counts.

00:04:15.205 --> 00:04:16.205
THESEUS: Newt.

00:04:18.416 --> 00:04:21.252
Mr. Scamander, it's clear
you're frustrated,

00:04:21.419 --> 00:04:24.421
and, frankly, so are we.

00:04:26.508 --> 00:04:30.052
In the spirit of compromise,
we'd like to make a proposition.

00:04:30.512 --> 00:04:31.929
What kind of proposition?

00:04:32.097 --> 00:04:35.641
The committee will agree to lift
your travel ban under one condition.

00:04:35.976 --> 00:04:37.768
SPIELMAN: You join the Ministry.

00:04:38.770 --> 00:04:41.438
Specifically, your brother's department.

00:04:44.734 --> 00:04:45.734
No.

00:04:47.195 --> 00:04:49.280
(STAMMERS) I think that...

00:04:49.698 --> 00:04:51.407
Theseus is the Auror.

00:04:51.825 --> 00:04:53.284
I think my talents lie elsewhere.

00:04:53.451 --> 00:04:54.702
GUZMAN: Mr. Scamander,

00:04:54.870 --> 00:04:58.289
the wizarding and non-wizarding worlds
have been at peace for over a century.

00:04:59.332 --> 00:05:01.917
Grindelwald wants to see
that peace destroyed.

00:05:02.085 --> 00:05:04.795
And for certain members
of our community,

00:05:04.963 --> 00:05:07.548
his message is very seductive.

00:05:08.884 --> 00:05:12.136
Many pure-bloods believe
it is their birthright to rule.

00:05:13.054 --> 00:05:17.016
Not only our world
but the non-magic world as well.

00:05:18.059 --> 00:05:24.148
They see Grindelwald as their hero,
and Grindelwald sees this boy

00:05:24.232 --> 00:05:26.525
as a means to make this all come true.

00:05:28.945 --> 00:05:31.655
I'm sorry. You're talking about Credence
as if he were still here.

00:05:32.866 --> 00:05:34.617
He survived, Newt.

00:05:36.620 --> 00:05:37.953
He's still alive.

00:05:38.788 --> 00:05:40.289
He left New York months ago.

00:05:40.790 --> 00:05:43.542
He's somewhere in Europe.
Where exactly, we don't know, but...

00:05:43.710 --> 00:05:45.711
NEWT: You want me to hunt Credence down?

00:05:47.422 --> 00:05:48.714
To kill him?

00:05:48.882 --> 00:05:51.050
Same old Scamander.

00:05:53.595 --> 00:05:54.929
What is he doing here?

00:05:55.013 --> 00:05:58.015
I'm taking on the job
that you're too soft to do.

00:06:01.978 --> 00:06:03.604
Is that it?

00:06:07.817 --> 00:06:10.402
- Travel documentation denied.
- (DOOR OPENS)

00:06:13.114 --> 00:06:14.448
Newt!

00:06:15.325 --> 00:06:17.409
You think I like the idea of Grimmson
any more than you do?

00:06:17.577 --> 00:06:19.078
Listen, I don't want to hear how
the ends justify the means, Theseus.

00:06:19.245 --> 00:06:21.163
I think you're gonna have to pull
your head out the sand!

00:06:21.331 --> 00:06:23.374
Okay, right, here we go.
What a selfish, irresponsible...

00:06:23.541 --> 00:06:29.171
The time is coming when everyone
is gonna have to pick a side.

00:06:29.339 --> 00:06:30.589
Even you.

00:06:31.383 --> 00:06:33.092
I don't do sides.

00:06:34.844 --> 00:06:36.053
(THESEUS SIGHS)

00:06:37.347 --> 00:06:39.723
Newt. Newt.

00:06:45.146 --> 00:06:46.480
Come here.

00:06:53.530 --> 00:06:54.822
They're watching you.

00:07:06.751 --> 00:07:08.085
GRIMMSON: Well, gentlemen...

00:07:09.462 --> 00:07:11.755
I assume this means I have the job.

